.TH tapectl-backend-add 1  "tapectl-backend-add " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-backend\-add \- Add an LTO tape drive to the config
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl backend add\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-name\fR> <\fB\-\-device\-tape\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-device\-sg\fR> [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-media\-type\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-capacity\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-enospc\-buffer\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an LTO tape drive to the config
.PP
Writes a validated `[[backends.lto]]` block, appended so existing comments survive. Find your drive with `ls \-l /dev/tape/by\-id/`, and `lsscsi \-g` for the sg node. Prefer the by\-id paths: /dev/nstN numbering is not stable across reboots.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name for this drive, used to select it later. Letters, digits, dot, underscore and dash
.TP
\fB\-\-device\-tape\fR \fI<DEVICE_TAPE>\fR
Tape device node, e.g. /dev/tape/by\-id/scsi\-XXXX\-nst
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-device\-sg\fR \fI<DEVICE_SG>\fR
SCSI generic node used for health/MAM queries, e.g. /dev/sg1
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-media\-type\fR \fI<MEDIA_TYPE>\fR [default: LTO\-6]
Media type, e.g. LTO\-6
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\fR \fI<CAPACITY>\fR [default: 2.5TB]
Uncompressed nominal capacity, e.g. 2.5TB
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-enospc\-buffer\fR \fI<ENOSPC_BUFFER>\fR
Headroom reserved before end\-of\-tape, e.g. 50M
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
